WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:04.720
Well, usually before you go to the bed, you have to take him to do pee pee.

00:04.720 --> 00:06.040
Yeah, we did.

00:06.040 --> 00:09.400
But I guess he still got nervous when he was in the car.

00:09.400 --> 00:12.240
And he likes to stick his head out the window.

00:12.240 --> 00:12.920
¿Sí?

00:12.920 --> 00:13.800
Sí.

00:13.800 --> 00:16.520
Pero tengan cuidado porque se puede salir.

00:16.520 --> 00:18.040
No, because we put it really high, high enough for only his head.

00:18.040 --> 00:19.120
Sometimes he might put his feet.

00:19.120 --> 00:20.120
Un pedacito de cristal.

00:20.120 --> 00:23.840
But he can't get out.

00:23.840 --> 00:26.400
Y nada más con un pedacito chiquitico de cristal.

00:26.400 --> 00:30.760
No, it's about, um, his hands could touch the top.

00:30.760 --> 00:33.440
And it's high enough for him to put his hands.

00:33.440 --> 00:34.600
And do you hold him?

00:34.600 --> 00:38.560
Yeah, I hold him. But I think that they're high enough so that él no se...

00:38.560 --> 00:42.160
Paula, be careful, because si él ve un gato or something,

00:42.160 --> 00:46.320
he might jump out of the car after the cat.

00:46.320 --> 00:46.960
Chill.

00:46.960 --> 00:48.080
Be careful.

00:48.080 --> 00:51.400
Yeah, but I don't think, because he sees people all the time in the cars.

00:51.400 --> 00:54.320
Sí, people, sí. But he never has seen a cat.

00:54.400 --> 00:56.160
Tú te imaginas si ve un gato.

00:56.160 --> 00:56.880
¿Qué pasa?

00:56.880 --> 00:58.280
He's seen one before.

00:58.280 --> 00:59.680
Well, you never know.

00:59.680 --> 01:00.920
You have to be careful.

01:00.920 --> 01:01.400
I know.

01:01.400 --> 01:05.400
Well, tell me, ¿qué pasó con el voleibol ese tuyo?

01:05.400 --> 01:08.200
¿Cómo fue? Que tú has entrado en el team de voleibol, muchacha.

01:08.200 --> 01:11.160
¿Quién te enseñó a ti a jugar a voleibol?

01:11.160 --> 01:12.000
I don't know.

01:12.000 --> 01:13.400
Yo creo que es una pasión.

01:13.400 --> 01:15.480
It's like, it's a passion already for me.

01:15.480 --> 01:18.200
Did you play volleyball at the other school you were in?

01:18.200 --> 01:20.520
We did. Pero it was completely different.

01:20.520 --> 01:21.400
It didn't work out.

01:21.400 --> 01:23.800
They changed the entire game.

01:24.560 --> 01:26.640
Did they have a team there?

01:26.640 --> 01:27.440
In my old school?

01:27.440 --> 01:29.600
Yeah, they did.

01:29.600 --> 01:33.400
And, tú sabes, it wasn't the same.

01:33.400 --> 01:37.400
Pero now I actually get to go into a team where I actually

01:37.400 --> 01:39.440
get to play the game.

01:39.440 --> 01:43.240
And you know, I was so nervous. Because I wasn't sure if I was gonna

01:43.240 --> 01:46.440
be able to, you know, entrar el team,

01:46.440 --> 01:48.720
like if I was gonna make it.

01:48.720 --> 01:52.680
Because I was around so many like awesome players.

01:52.680 --> 01:54.800
Y ya fueron.

01:54.800 --> 01:58.400
Pero me dijo tu mamá con la niña que before was in the team, she didn't make it?

01:58.400 --> 01:59.400
She didn't make it.

01:59.400 --> 02:00.280
How come?

02:00.280 --> 02:01.160
I don't know.

02:01.160 --> 02:03.800
I think it was because she wasn't doing so good.

02:03.800 --> 02:06.080
I'm not sure, 'cause maybe that's what they thought.

02:06.080 --> 02:08.880
Pero I thought ella fue like very good.

02:08.880 --> 02:09.760
¿Ella fue buena jugando?

02:09.760 --> 02:11.000
Sí, fue buena, muy buena.

02:11.000 --> 02:11.720
¿Buena?

02:11.720 --> 02:14.080
¿Y por qué no la cogieron?

02:14.080 --> 02:16.800
Maybe it was be... I don't know, maybe it was because

02:16.800 --> 02:18.760
that she had her grades low.

02:18.760 --> 02:23.000
Because if you have an F, or maybe more than one F,

02:23.000 --> 02:26.520
you can't go into the team.

02:26.520 --> 02:28.760
Maybe. But maybe that's not the reason.

02:28.760 --> 02:30.200
Maybe they just didn't like her.

02:30.200 --> 02:31.680
Or maybe they had better players.

02:31.680 --> 02:33.800
And when do you have to practice?

02:33.800 --> 02:37.760
We have to practice, uh, every week, um, school day.

02:37.760 --> 02:40.320
Monday, Tuesday, Thursday, and Friday.

02:40.320 --> 02:42.120
I mean, Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Thursday, and Friday.

02:42.120 --> 02:43.800
¿Y a qué hora?

02:43.800 --> 02:47.080
Monday, Tuesday, Thursday, and Friday at seven forty-five.

02:47.120 --> 02:49.800
Seven forty-five in the morning?

02:49.800 --> 02:50.400
Yes.

02:50.400 --> 02:52.000
And who's gonna take you?

02:52.000 --> 02:53.680
I will, if nobody will take you.

02:53.680 --> 02:55.480
Look, I'm not gonna get up that early.

02:55.480 --> 02:58.040
No, probably mami and papi.

02:58.040 --> 02:58.640
Ah, bueno, sí.

02:58.640 --> 03:01.640
Porque papi va temprano para trabajo.

03:01.640 --> 03:04.880
Y te deja ahí. Cuando te deja, ¿hay gente en la escuela?

03:04.880 --> 03:07.160
Well, there will be other girls that are on the team there

03:07.160 --> 03:07.640
waiting.

03:07.640 --> 03:08.840
¿Y la maestra?

03:08.840 --> 03:10.960
She'll be coming in at the same time.

03:10.960 --> 03:12.960
Paula, y...

03:12.960 --> 03:15.320
There are teachers coming in at that time already.

03:15.320 --> 03:15.960
Oh, they do?

03:15.960 --> 03:17.240
Yeah, but they're not there outside.

03:17.240 --> 03:18.840
They're inside preparing for school to start.

03:18.840 --> 03:19.480
Inside the building?

03:19.480 --> 03:20.120
Yeah.

03:20.120 --> 03:22.680
And we're outside.

03:22.680 --> 03:25.960
And how do you get through the office when you go outside?

03:25.960 --> 03:28.520
Well, we go through the bus loop.

03:28.520 --> 03:31.480
And the parents drop us off there.

03:31.480 --> 03:33.720
What's the bus loop?

03:33.720 --> 03:37.440
Where the bus is for the kids that go on the bus.

03:37.440 --> 03:38.440
They drop the kids off.

03:38.440 --> 03:40.720
Where I leave you every morning?

03:40.720 --> 03:41.640
The same place I leave you?

03:41.640 --> 03:44.680
No, on the other side.

03:44.680 --> 03:49.080
¿Dónde los niños juegan por la tablita esa?

03:49.080 --> 03:50.240
¿La patineta esa que yo veo?

03:50.240 --> 03:53.800
Oh, no, no, no, the other side where all the buses are.

03:53.800 --> 03:55.000
Oh, in the back.

03:55.000 --> 03:56.840
Yeah.

03:56.840 --> 03:58.200
That way we're closer to the school.

03:58.200 --> 04:00.320
And I don't have to walk that far.

04:00.320 --> 04:03.640
¿Y después, de qué hora a qué hora vas a hacer la práctica?

04:03.640 --> 04:04.880
It's an hour.

04:04.880 --> 04:06.320
So if I start at seven forty-five, I end at eight forty-five.

04:06.320 --> 04:08.920
¿Y después se pueden bañar ahí?

04:08.920 --> 04:09.880
I don't think so.

04:09.880 --> 04:11.640
¿Y ustedes llevan ropa para cambiarse?

04:11.640 --> 04:14.280
Yeah, the school clothes.

04:14.280 --> 04:15.760
Imagínate qué rollo.

04:15.760 --> 04:18.960
¿Tiene que llevar la ropa en un puchero?

04:18.960 --> 04:21.560
No, we just stick 'em in our book bags.

04:21.560 --> 04:23.080
Bueno, ¿un jean?

04:23.080 --> 04:26.080
Jean and a polo shirt.

04:26.080 --> 04:29.840
Y entonces para la práctica, ¿qué llevas? ¿Un short y un t-shirt?

04:29.840 --> 04:33.080
We are gonna take the shorts and any type of shirt

04:33.080 --> 04:35.160
with our knee pads.

04:35.160 --> 04:36.320
Ay, ay, yo vi los kneepads.

04:36.320 --> 04:38.000
Son como unos elásticos, ¿no, Paula?

04:38.000 --> 04:38.400
Yeah.

04:38.400 --> 04:41.600
Yo pensé que eran sobre un casco plástico duro.

04:41.640 --> 04:42.520
You're crazy!

04:46.120 --> 04:48.640
Yeah, but that's not the same, because if you go on the floor,

04:48.640 --> 04:51.640
you can really hurt yourself with those.

04:51.640 --> 04:53.000
Es más que hurt yourself.

04:53.000 --> 04:55.440
Probably you can hurt the wood in that place.

04:55.440 --> 04:56.320
That's why.

04:56.320 --> 04:58.360
Sí, donde juegan béisbol, básquetbol, ¿no?

04:58.360 --> 04:59.480
Yeah.

04:59.480 --> 04:59.960
Oh.

05:03.040 --> 05:06.280
So I'm not gonna be seeing you every morning then?

05:06.280 --> 05:07.000
No.

05:07.000 --> 05:08.440
Only Wednesdays?

05:08.440 --> 05:10.800
Only Wednesdays and maybe on the weekends.

05:10.840 --> 05:12.360
Maybe on weekends.

05:12.360 --> 05:14.400
So who's gonna fix your breakfast?

05:14.400 --> 05:15.720
Who's gonna fix your lunch?

05:15.720 --> 05:17.520
Bueno, I'm probably gonna

05:17.520 --> 05:19.680
have to start eating at the school.

05:19.680 --> 05:21.400
Breakfast and lunch?

05:21.400 --> 05:22.640
Only Wednesdays.

05:22.640 --> 05:24.960
Only Wednesdays you can make me lunch.

05:24.960 --> 05:31.120
Entonces then I will not be buying any stuff for you this weekend.

05:31.120 --> 05:33.600
OK, Monday you're gonna go to practice?

05:33.600 --> 05:36.200
OK, so Wednesday is the only day.

05:36.200 --> 05:39.440
And what I do, I get you a little bit of ham

05:39.480 --> 05:40.880
and maybe a croissant.

05:40.880 --> 05:41.480
Sí.

05:41.480 --> 05:42.800
Un cruasán.

05:42.800 --> 05:46.840
Y la papita, y la jugo de manzana, y agüita.

05:46.840 --> 05:47.320
Oh my god.

05:47.320 --> 05:48.080
Agüita, Paula, ¿no la beben, agüita?

05:48.080 --> 05:49.600
Maybe I can take some agüitas to you.

05:49.600 --> 05:52.080
And you can put it in your bag.

05:52.080 --> 05:54.440
Maybe.

05:54.440 --> 05:55.400
Oh my goodness, abuela.

05:55.400 --> 05:57.400
Everything hurts.

05:57.400 --> 05:59.040
Everything hurts?

05:59.040 --> 06:00.000
Everything hurts.

06:00.000 --> 06:00.960
You're an old lady.

06:00.960 --> 06:02.080
I know I am.

06:02.080 --> 06:02.960
A qué voleibol ese...

06:02.960 --> 06:04.880
¿Te duele el cucu?

06:04.880 --> 06:05.680
Everything hurts.

06:05.680 --> 06:06.960
Yes, that too.

06:06.960 --> 06:08.440
That too?

06:08.440 --> 06:09.120
Mi madre.

06:09.120 --> 06:11.520
Estás muy grave. Estás en bad shape.

06:11.520 --> 06:14.520
I think it was because I did thirty squats

06:14.520 --> 06:16.280
and I haven't done squats in forever.

06:16.280 --> 06:18.280
¿Qué cosas son los squats?

06:18.280 --> 06:21.520
Well, you have to bend your knees and go up and down.

06:21.520 --> 06:22.480
A ver, show me.

06:22.480 --> 06:23.320
Be careful!

06:23.320 --> 06:23.920
Be careful.

06:23.920 --> 06:25.200
Show me.

06:25.200 --> 06:25.680
Show me.

06:25.680 --> 06:26.680
OK.

06:26.680 --> 06:27.680
One.

06:27.680 --> 06:29.360
Ah, y ¿para qué es eso?

06:29.360 --> 06:31.160
It's good because it makes your muscles stronger

06:31.160 --> 06:35.800
and it keeps you in shape.

06:35.800 --> 06:36.840
Yo creo que eso también te va a hacer crecer el cucu.

06:36.840 --> 06:39.920
Yo te veo.

06:39.920 --> 06:42.120
OK, abuela.

06:42.120 --> 06:44.120
Random.

06:44.120 --> 06:45.120
Oye, y las niñas que están en el team,

06:47.640 --> 06:49.520
¿hay algunas que son very close friends of yours, or no?

06:49.520 --> 06:52.320
Well, the one that was supposed to make it on the team, she was,

06:52.320 --> 06:54.440
but no.

06:54.440 --> 06:55.840
I think I only have one friend.

06:55.840 --> 06:58.720
One friend in the team?

06:58.720 --> 07:00.240
¿Y hay muchos negritos?

07:00.240 --> 07:02.840
There's only two.

07:02.840 --> 07:04.480
¿Dos negritas?

07:04.480 --> 07:06.120
Are they your friends?

07:06.200 --> 07:07.440
No, I don't know them.

07:07.440 --> 07:08.920
Y do you have any classes with them?

07:08.920 --> 07:10.640
No.

07:10.640 --> 07:11.920
Nadie en el team tú tienes clase?

07:11.920 --> 07:14.360
Well, um, with one of them I do.

07:14.360 --> 07:17.080
So...

07:20.240 --> 07:21.240
Cuéntame, ¿cómo a ti te gusta el colegio este?

07:21.240 --> 07:23.480
¿Cómo tú comparas este colegio con el colegio anterior?

07:23.480 --> 07:26.400
How do you like it?

07:26.400 --> 07:27.880
I like it.

07:27.880 --> 07:29.320
It's better than my old school.

07:29.320 --> 07:32.040
Y the people are so much nicer.

07:32.040 --> 07:35.280
They are nicer here?

07:35.320 --> 07:36.320
Yes.

07:36.320 --> 07:37.400
Who, the teachers or the children?

07:37.400 --> 07:38.840
No, everybody.

07:38.840 --> 07:39.680
Really?

07:39.680 --> 07:40.520
Yeah.

07:40.520 --> 07:41.360
It's a lot tougher.

07:41.360 --> 07:42.880
A lot tougher.

07:42.880 --> 07:44.080
You mean the material?

07:44.080 --> 07:46.720
Educational.

07:46.720 --> 07:49.480
Um, no, no, no, the, um...

07:49.480 --> 07:52.720
The curriculum.

07:52.720 --> 07:57.120
Yeah, the curriculum is harder, a lot harder.

07:57.120 --> 08:00.640
Testing, not as much as before.

08:00.640 --> 08:02.800
OK.

08:02.800 --> 08:03.640
Less testing.

08:03.640 --> 08:06.440
Pero more projects.

08:06.440 --> 08:08.280
You had more testing than here?

08:08.280 --> 08:10.800
Yeah. We don't have to do spelling in this school.

08:10.800 --> 08:11.280
No?

08:11.280 --> 08:14.320
At all.

08:14.320 --> 08:15.360
Don't you have any class that say spelling?

08:15.360 --> 08:16.920
No.

08:16.920 --> 08:17.920
Y tú ¿cómo tú aprendes el spelling de las palabras?

08:17.920 --> 08:19.440
We don't have it.

08:19.440 --> 08:22.720
Do you have history?

08:22.720 --> 08:26.160
We have geography.

08:26.160 --> 08:27.640
¿Y historia?

08:27.640 --> 08:30.480
No, we have geography.

08:30.480 --> 08:31.480
It's more like the map of the countries.

08:31.480 --> 08:34.800
Sí.

08:34.800 --> 08:36.880
It's not as much about history.

08:36.880 --> 08:38.640
It's not like we're learning about George Washington

08:38.640 --> 08:42.560
and Abraham Lincoln.

08:42.560 --> 08:45.600
And we're learning more about cultures this year

08:45.600 --> 08:47.960
and different cultures from different countries and continents.

08:47.960 --> 08:48.680
Like the other day we were learning about Russia.

08:48.680 --> 08:50.760
Mmhm.

08:50.760 --> 08:51.840
¿Y qué aprendiste?

08:51.840 --> 08:54.160
Um...

08:54.160 --> 08:57.600
Aparte de que los rusos no se bañan.

08:57.600 --> 08:59.480
They don't?

08:59.520 --> 09:01.720
No, they don't, because it's very, very cold where they live.

09:01.720 --> 09:02.920
And usually they don't bath every day.

09:02.920 --> 09:05.600
I have a friend...

09:05.600 --> 09:08.400
Maybe they bath once a week.

09:08.400 --> 09:09.400
I have a friend...

09:09.400 --> 09:12.440
Even if we are lucky.

09:12.440 --> 09:13.560
I have a friend from Russia.

09:13.560 --> 09:14.840
If she lives here, es distinto.

09:14.840 --> 09:15.520
Porque entonces ya se baña, porque aquí calor.

09:15.520 --> 09:16.880
Yeah, she lives in New York.

09:16.880 --> 09:18.360
And I met her on the cruise.

09:18.360 --> 09:22.840
Do you remember the one we went on?

09:22.840 --> 09:25.760
Oh, which cruise?

09:25.760 --> 09:31.720
In the one from, um, the Royal Caribbean.

09:31.720 --> 09:34.400
Oh, the, el, el de Freedom?

09:34.400 --> 09:36.920
Yeah, that one.

09:36.920 --> 09:39.200
The Freedom?

09:39.200 --> 09:41.200
We had fun there.

09:41.200 --> 09:41.920
It was fun.

09:41.920 --> 09:42.680
Oh, yeah.

09:42.680 --> 09:43.640
And I liked that thing, that board thingy, the Flowrider.

09:43.640 --> 09:44.680
Mhmm.

09:44.680 --> 09:45.200
When I got on my knees, it was so much fun.

09:45.200 --> 09:46.320
Y em, yeah...

09:46.320 --> 09:47.480
Y the people there were so nice on the cruise.

09:47.480 --> 09:50.840
Y la comida, the pizza there was awesome.

09:50.840 --> 09:51.920
Yeah, remember how much pizza we ate?

09:51.920 --> 09:53.480
And it was like an all you can eat pizza.

09:53.520 --> 09:57.800
Y la galletica.

09:57.800 --> 09:58.680
La galletica.

09:58.680 --> 10:00.760
Oh my god.

10:00.760 --> 10:05.720
¿Te acuerdas todas las galleticas que trajimos a abuela?

10:05.720 --> 10:06.880
Yeah.

10:06.880 --> 10:08.920
Que guardamos galleticas.

10:08.920 --> 10:09.920
Trajimos galleticas a abuela.

10:09.920 --> 10:12.400
And the desserts.

10:12.400 --> 10:14.400
They had a tiramisú.

10:14.400 --> 10:15.880
Tiramisú.

10:15.880 --> 10:17.400
Which one did you like best, the Freedom or the one that we went, Costa, at the end of the year?

10:17.400 --> 10:19.080
Fortuna?

10:19.080 --> 10:20.960
The Fortuna.

10:20.960 --> 10:22.400
Um, I liked Freedom more.

10:22.400 --> 10:23.080
But I liked the food in Fortuna more.

10:23.120 --> 10:24.040
Fortuna was good.

10:24.040 --> 10:25.760
La comida fue...

10:25.760 --> 10:27.920
Maravillosa.

10:27.920 --> 10:31.680
Maravillosa.

10:31.680 --> 10:33.600
Como comimos tan rico.

10:33.600 --> 10:34.560
Mhmm.

10:34.560 --> 10:35.680
Oh, I'm getting hungry.

10:35.680 --> 10:36.400
Yeah.

10:36.400 --> 10:38.760
Ah, no.

10:38.760 --> 10:39.480
Definitely not.

10:39.480 --> 10:44.080
I think we ate so much this morning.

10:44.080 --> 10:45.040
It wasn't not even funny.

10:45.040 --> 10:47.080
Are you feeling OK now?

10:47.080 --> 10:48.120
Better.

10:48.120 --> 10:49.680
OK, good.

10:49.680 --> 10:50.200
Pero la comida, los pancakes de blueberry.

10:50.200 --> 10:51.280
Después con el hash brown casserole, two sunny side up eggs.

10:51.280 --> 10:53.560
Las tostadas.

10:53.560 --> 10:59.080
Las tostadas.

10:59.080 --> 11:01.920
Y jugo de naranja.

11:01.920 --> 11:07.160
Y jugo de naranja.

11:07.160 --> 11:11.160
Oh god.

11:11.160 --> 11:12.840
But then fuimos a caminar por el mall.

11:12.840 --> 11:16.120
Y entonces se te bajó la comida.

11:16.120 --> 11:19.080
Oh goodness, I wish I was still there.

11:19.120 --> 11:26.600
Ay, como bien bonito, Paula.

11:26.600 --> 11:27.920
Yeah.

11:27.920 --> 11:28.920
I loved the stores there.

11:28.920 --> 11:29.920
Son todos diferentes.

11:29.920 --> 11:31.360
Y el em, fuimos a Love Culture que estaba bonito.

11:31.360 --> 11:36.280
Mhmm.

11:36.280 --> 11:37.120
Fuimos a Zoomies.

11:37.120 --> 11:39.200
Em, fuimos al Coldwater Creek.

11:39.200 --> 11:40.040
A Coldwater.

11:40.040 --> 11:40.720
Mhmm.

11:40.720 --> 11:43.520
Y ah, Origins.

11:43.520 --> 11:45.440
Em, ¿cuál otra?

11:45.440 --> 11:48.800
Yo creo que eso fue.

11:48.800 --> 11:50.960
No, y fuimos también al lugar ese de la aprendecita.

11:50.960 --> 11:53.440
¿Briden?

11:53.440 --> 11:54.480
¿Burkden o algo así?

11:54.480 --> 11:58.360
Y también we were outside looking window shopping in Black and White.

11:58.360 --> 12:03.080
Ay, Black and White.

12:03.080 --> 12:04.320
Y Ann Taylor.

12:04.320 --> 12:09.200
Ann Taylor Loft.

12:09.200 --> 12:11.800
Oh, that Black and White, the dress.

12:11.800 --> 12:15.040
That black, black dress, oh.

12:15.080 --> 12:16.200
That black dress with the...

12:16.200 --> 12:19.680
Yes.

12:19.680 --> 12:24.720
It was beautiful.

